    <blockquote class="excerpt"><p><strong>RQ-INTERCEPT.</strong> Higher poisoning rates of the training dataset result in a delayed intercept, even if the active learning rate is much higher than the poisoning rate. This also corresponds to the diminishing returns in the reduction of time to intercept for increasing active learning rates.</p></blockquote>

    <h3>Stability of Passive Recovery</h3>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Throughout the three classifiers, we see comparable stability in passive recovery, with an overall average recovery rate of 55% in all classifiers, settings, and tolerance margins. For the tolerance margins 0.00, 0.01, and 0.05, the average recovery rate is 42%, 53%, and 70%, respectively. The comparable average recovery rate between classifiers under the same tolerance margin shows that the choice of classifier does not have a significant impact on the stability of recovery rate across multiple settings. The varying average recovery rate of the different tolerance margins shows the importance of considering the tolerance requirement for an application, as passive recovery may be sufficient under certain tolerance margins, but insufficient under others.</p>
    </div>

